  {
    "sha": "8dd88115d443c2b6d98e80db141d04ba4c7fcbf3",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDhkZDg4MTE1ZDQ0M2MyYjZkOThlODBkYjE0MWQwNGJhNGM3ZmNiZjM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T14:47:09Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T14:47:09Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): never write an arc block whose written ends coincide\n\nAn arc record shorter than the output step (a 1 um arc in inch, or a\nsub-micrometre arc in mm) was written as G02/G03 with the same X/Y as\nits start and a nonzero I/J: a control reads that block as a full\ncircle. Each shipped post now asks one PRELUDE helper, arcFate\n(crates/post/src/post/arc_guard.rs), with its own word format: the arc\nposts as before when its written ends differ or it turns more than half\na circle; a short arc under the step posts as the post's straight move\nwhen Z (a helix) or a rotary still moves, and as no block otherwise.\nKlartext no longer refuses the short case. The R-word mode is after the\nguard.\n\nPinned by coincident_arcs.rs: the reporter's tiny.cnc (Fanuc inch), a\ntable over all 20 shipped posts in mm and inch (and R mode), the metric\nthree-decimal collision and a short resolvable R arc. radius_arcs'\ntiny_inch case now expects no arc block (its I/J block was the fault).\n\nFixes #3442\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
