      },
      "message": "fix(post): keep centreless arcs to their scripts and read a noisy full turn as full\n\nAfter the second read of #3471:\n- arcFateOf returns \"arc\" when the record states no finite centre, so\n  each script's own refusal by name still runs.\n- Ends within 1e-5 mm in the stream (the band of emitArcWithRadius) are\n  a full turn stated as one record, so float noise never turns a full\n  helical turn into a straight Z move. tinyg and the heidenhain chord\n  path use the same band for their own sweep.\n- New pins: the rule's answers through the PRELUDE, a noisy full helix\n  in every mill post, a near-full turn with coincident written ends as\n  the dialect's full circle, and a short arc with an A word.\n\nRefs #3442\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
